<SiteLayout title="About" description="Why Pranam Bihar exists and how we tell Bihar’s stories." eyebrow="Why Pranam Bihar" heading="A new way to see Bihar." intro="An independent editorial home for the people, places, knowledge and living culture that make Bihar extraordinary.">
  <section class="collection"><div class="wrap prose"><p>Bihar is often spoken about through a narrow set of headlines. But no place with this much history, talent and cultural depth can fit inside a stereotype. Pranam Bihar begins with a simple belief: better stories can widen what people imagine about a place—and what a place imagines for itself.</p><h2>Curiosity before cliché.</h2><p>We document Bihar with care: its centres of knowledge, food, languages, landscapes, living traditions and the everyday work of its people. We will be proud without becoming uncritical, and historical without treating Bihar as a museum.</p><h2>Inheritance and possibility.</h2><p>Tradition and modernity are not opposing teams. Our six editorial pillars connect place, food, culture, people and history with the ideas and systems shaping Bihar now.</p><h2>Built to grow.</h2><p>This website is organised as a living publication. Stories will deepen into collections, places into practical guides, and profiles into a sourced archive of remarkable lives.</p><p><a href="/editorial-standards/"><strong>Read our editorial and corrections standards →</strong></a></p><div class="note"><blockquote>“To tell better stories about a place is to imagine a better future for it.”</blockquote></div></div></section>
</SiteLayout>
